Z||000003||Nashco||05-06-2001||03:45 PM||||Hey, perfect timing, I've been searching for the same thing.  I found that some of the stock dogbone frames won't allow bushing to be inserted because they have a ridge on the inside of them.  I thought mine could be used to insert bushings into, but looked closely and it was useless for that <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  All the 2.5s and the 85-86 2.8s came with a dogbone that had a round hole that can be used to put poly in.  I got a housing that is identical to the 85/86 but is aftermarket-powdercoated TIG welded steel. (I got it from Darrell Morse  <A HREF="mailto:morse86@aol.com">morse86@aol.com</A>  for a killer deal because he didn't have the poly for them yet).<P>Anyway, he told me of the two places that have the poly that are a direct insert.  The first one is here at <A HREF="http://www.suspension.com/fiero-prothane.htm" TARGET=_blank>Suspension.com's Fiero Stuff</A> for 20 bucks and they have them in stock.  The other is at <A HREF="http://www.secureleadercom.com/store/prodinfo_pegasus.asp?number=52897&variation=&aitem=3&mitem=9" TARGET=_blank>The Fiero Store</A> for 25 bucks, and I've been told they stock them as well.<P>I'm going to order mine from suspension.com this week, as I need them badly.  The only thing I don't like about the suspension.com website is the ordering method.  I'm just going to call my order in, as I have to with the Fiero Store anyway (different shipping address from billing address).<P>Phew...why did I make that so long?  Hope this helps.  That should be all you need if you have one of the above years.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000004||c m west||05-06-2001||03:51 PM||||our website will answer all of your questions<BR> <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A> <P>Eric - West Coast Fiero||||reg||1
Z||000005||Nashco||05-06-2001||04:00 PM||||Eric, your sight didn't answer all my questions, it actually made me have more <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  Your transmission mounts don't say what they apply to; do they fit all years/models?  Is it powdercoated or painted?  I was also curious what durometer you use.  I know that it's not a huge deal, but I am curious.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
