Z||000011||Taijiguy||05-14-2001||08:19 AM||||Prothane has about the best prices around for the bushings. I didn't see the cradle mounts for an 88 listed, but they probably have them. Cradle mounts for 84-87 are about 43 bucks, front control arm sets are about the same, and rear control arm sets for 84-87 are about 23 bucks. They have rear bushings listed for the 88 for 54 bucks.<A HREF="http://www.prothanesuspension.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.prothanesuspension.com</A> <BR>Fiero parts are towards the bottom of the page. Call them about the 88 cradle mounts.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Taijiguy (edited 05-14-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000012||Will||05-14-2001||12:18 PM||||The '88 cradle is hard mounted--it doesn't use cradle bushings.||||reg||1
Z||000013||c m west||05-14-2001||04:10 PM||||All of our mounts work with any and all ( every year ) stock fiero transmission ever produced - that is why there is a general discription, because they will work on everything||||reg||1
